## PHASE 2 — ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS
The root cause of the data loss upon logout is a combination of two critical synchronization failures—resulting in a completely **Faux-Implemented Backend Persistence**:

1. **Frontend State Not Fully Bootstrapped**: When a user logs in, [BootGuard.tsx](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/components/layout/BootGuard.tsx) checks auth and correctly retrieves the User profile from Supabase, but it completely skips bootstrapping the rest of the game state (Quests, Messages, Journal, Equipment, etc.) by returning early and bypassing the comprehensive [initializeFromDB()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/stores/useGameStore.ts#228-272) action in `useGameStore`.
2. **Nullified Cloud Saves**: `useGameStore` automatically attempts to backup the user's data upon state changes using bulk saves ([saveMessages](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/services/supabaseDB.ts#116-126), [saveQuests](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/services/supabaseDB.ts#188-196)). However, in [src/services/supabaseDB.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/services/supabaseDB.ts), these bulk save functions are hardcoded to skip the Supabase insertion entirely and only write to IndexedDB (`localDB`). 
   - A comment in the code assumes individual items are saved singly, but the singular save functions (`.saveMessage()`, `.saveQuest()`) are **never actually called** anywhere in the application.

When a user logs out, [Settings.tsx](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/pages/Settings.tsx) triggers `localDB.clearAll()`, completely wiping out all stored gameplay data which, unbeknownst to the user, was never actually sent to the cloud.

## PHASE 3 — DATA FLOW AUDIT
Here is exactly where persistence breaks during the data lifecycle:
- **Login**: [Login.tsx](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/pages/Login.tsx) fetches `db.getUser`, sets it in Zustand, and redirects to `/terminal`.
- **Session Creation**: [BootGuard.tsx](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/components/layout/BootGuard.tsx) intercepts, refetches `db.getUser` from Supabase, and mounts the app.
- **Data Retrieval (BREAK 1)**: Fails to load historical messages, quests, or journals because [BootGuard](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/components/layout/BootGuard.tsx#9-60) and [Login](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/pages/Login.tsx#26-416) do not trigger [initializeFromDB()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/stores/useGameStore.ts#228-272) for returning users.
- **Gameplay Usage (BREAK 2)**: The user plays, generating quests and messages. `useGameStore`'s subscription fires [persistToDB()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/stores/useGameStore.ts#292-301). This calls `db.saveQuests(bulk)` which routes *only* to `localDB`. Supabase never receives the data arrays.
- **Logout**: `localDB.clearAll()` wipes all local data.
- **Next Login**: State resets, because Supabase only ever contained the baseline character profile logic.

## PHASE 4 — LONG-TERM ARCHITECTURE SOLUTION
To permanently guarantee user data persistence across sessions:
- **Database Persistence**: Ensure all game state arrays (Messages, Quests, Journals, Equipment, Abilities) are correctly bulk-upserted to their respective Supabase tables.
- **Batched Syncing**: Instead of abandoning bulk saves to Supabase, update [saveMessages](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/services/supabaseDB.ts#116-126), [saveQuests](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/services/supabaseDB.ts#188-196), and [saveJournals](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/services/supabaseDB.ts#237-244) in [supabaseDB.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/services/supabaseDB.ts) to execute array `upsert` queries to Supabase, effectively creating an automatic, seamless cloud-save system.
- **Complete Bootstrapping**: Modify [BootGuard.tsx](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/components/layout/BootGuard.tsx) and [Login.tsx](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/pages/Login.tsx) to fully invoke `useGameStore.initializeFromDB()` when an existing user is detected, guaranteeing the entire user state restores automatically from the cloud database.
- **Export/Import Obsolescence**: Local data export becomes purely a voluntary offline backup mechanism, rather than a required crutch.

## PHASE 5 — USER DATA SAFETY
To prevent future data loss and ensure seamless operations:
- **Automatic Cloud Save**: Implement continuous, debounced uploads of the Zustand state directly to Supabase.
- **Offline Merging**: Since `localDB` still exists, [initializeFromDB](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/vortex/WebApp/src/stores/useGameStore.ts#228-272) should prioritize the cloud timestamp, merging or completely overwriting local data if the cloud save is newer.

